questionvariables.text:
/* Shared Question Bank Place Value, Rounding and Standard Form PVRS-10
Adaptive remediation task: correct the misconception that a boundary digit of exactly 5 may be rounded down.
Reference-only interaction sources: NUMBAS-21514 NUMBAS-169559
This STACK question is independently authored. No source wording or mathematical content is copied. */
/* Choose the place being rounded.
1 = nearest ten 2 = nearest hundred 3 = nearest thousand */
place_choice: rand_with_prohib(1,3,[]);
place_value: if place_choice=1 then 10 elseif place_choice=2 then 100 else 1000;
place_name: if place_choice=1 then "ten" elseif place_choice=2 then "hundred" else "thousand";
/* Generate a safe positive base multiple.
The final number is exactly halfway between two consecutive multiples of the requested place value. */
base_index: rand_with_prohib( 120, 850, [] );
lower_multiple: base_index * place_value;
/* Exact halfway case.
Examples: 4650 to nearest hundred 72500 to nearest thousand */
number: lower_multiple + place_value/2;
/* School half-up answer.
At an exact 5 boundary, move to the upper multiple. */
answer: lower_multiple + place_value;
/* Primary misconception: round the exact 5 boundary downward.
This is also equivalent to truncation for these generated variants. */
wrong_round_down: lower_multiple;
/* A second common mistake is to add only 5 rather than respecting the target place. */
wrong_keep_five: lower_multiple + 5;
